spoint grass streaming stall ROOT FIX (profiler: prolandTerrainH/groundHeightLocal 68.8% under GrassPlacement.classify on the rAF). GrassPlacement.classify ALONE of the three scatter systems still sampled height FIRST (1 elev + 4 slope) before the density coin -> every cell paid 1-5 groundHeightLocal (~0.4ms each) even when coin-rejected. FIX 1: reorder to reject on grassDensity(temp,humidity,0) CEILING (grassDensity is monotonic-decreasing in slopeRatio, max at slope=0) BEFORE any height sample, same coin re-checked against the real slope-faded accept = bit-identical (grass is client-visual only, NO server-parity golden gate, so a self-contained output-identical test is the witness, not a byte-diff regen gate). ~24% fewer samples even fully-lush; rejected cells pay ZERO. FIX 2: a SINGLE pure classify reorder only cuts ~24% on lush ground - the worst-frame stall (witnessed maxUpdateMs 960ms) is one lush 256-cell chunk built atomically in one rAF; fixed with createGrassChunkCursor (resumable per-cell builder, injectable clock for testability) driven by a per-frame wall-clock budget (4ms, cfg.grassLoadBudgetMs) in Grass.streamRing, committing to InstancedMesh only when cursor.done (chunk stays all-or-nothing in `loaded`). Browser-witnessed singleplayer: maxUpdateMs 960->16ms, grass still inst:3017, fps 32-42, 0 errors. LESSON: a cheap-reject reorder caps the AVERAGE cost; an incremental wall-clock-budgeted builder caps the WORST single-frame cost - a perf complaint about a sync rAF stall usually needs BOTH (reduce total work AND spread the irreducible remainder across frames). Witness the worst case (maxUpdateMs across the whole stream) not just steady-state updateMs. Pre-existing VegPlacement.test.js water-margin failures are orthogonal (VegPlacement untouched; left flagged, not folded into a responsiveness-only slice - P12 value-per-risk).